Notebook[{
Cell["Hypermatrix", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"00c6a4cf-16d1-784f-a181-8f8083444bb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "87504a42-2a9b-644e-adba-3dd134842e6e"],
 " ",
 "represents the given arrays as a hypermatrix, holding them in canonical \
order."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"77ebad06-0fc0-614a-adbb-ecfb031ad36e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f4a50496-37a3-6b48-aed8-1d30a41c323b"],
 " ",
 "is equivalent."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"e67ca9f5-1dd5-5044-92e9-c16455f955e6"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"8d6f18ea-e32d-884d-bdc0-d83f2f43d22d"],

Cell["\<\
The arrays are ordered by array order, lowest first; then by dimensions, \
shorter first, compared term by term; then by symmetry, taking \"Symmetric\" \
before \"Cyclic\" before \"Rigid\".\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a04f42d8-9176-c341-8145-bd04cb3eb26e"],

Cell["\<\
Two arrays alike in all three are put in the Wolfram Language's own canonical \
order, so that a hypermatrix is a function of the set of arrays it was given \
and of nothing else. Giving the same arrays in a different order produces the \
identical expression.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e591d133-945b-ae44-aea8-a7df766837ac"],

Cell["\<\
An irregular array is necessarily \"Rigid\", since only a regular array can \
carry a symmetry, so the symmetry criterion separates the regular arrays \
among themselves.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b118f18c-9514-714a-b05d-36de0c496be9"],

Cell["\<\
Arrays of any kind of entry sit together freely. Raw entries given in place \
of an array are promoted to an ArrayObject.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"980b2e2b-8425-e344-b026-4a54b4188d42"],

Cell["\<\
Length gives the number of arrays, and Normal the entries of each of them in \
order.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2cb32562-1524-a343-88fb-4075538ec940"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"1296cb0d-61fa-8541-a5b7-a58e40f5efd8"],

Cell["The arrays are sorted whatever order they are given in:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"82a61dbc-7ad9-c548-a475-76872c9bf11b"],

Cell["\<\
hm = Hypermatrix[{
   ArrayObject[Array[1 &, {2, 2, 2}], \"Symmetric\"],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}],
   ArrayObject[{1, 2}],
   ArrayObject[{1, 2, 3}],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, \"Symmetric\"],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, \"Cyclic\"]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"00b4ef2c-09f9-594f-a9b3-40f73d79c8ec"],

